  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday) \nIssued at 118 AM MDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nOn Monday, scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms will\ncontinue over east central and southeast areas, where moist \nsoutheast low level return flow will develop as a weak trailing\ndisturbance crosses aloft. PWATs are forecast to trend downward, \nso the risk of additional flash flooding will be low. Otherwise, \ndrier and warmer weather is forecast Monday through midweek as an\nactive storm track north of NM draws dry west and southwest flow \nover the forecast area. Showers and thunderstorms may increase \nin coverage again across the forecast area Thursday and Friday, \ndepending on how much progress another upper level low pressure \nsystem can make advancing into the western US. At this time \nconfidence is low in another widespread rain event over the \nforecast area, due to significant and persistent differences in  \nmodel track and timing of the weather system.",
